<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78612" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παράπλοος</span></b> , 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραπλήρ-πλους</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>coasting voyage</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς Ἰταλίας καλῶς παράπλου κεῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.36
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν παράπλῳ κεῖσθαι</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				44
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.33
			</span></i>, etc. ; simply, <i>passage,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				POxy.
				525.1
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>VH</u>
				1.28
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>shore to be coasted along</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τραχὺς Πλατανιστὸς καλούμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					14.5.3
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				14.3.2
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ π. αὐτοῦ</span> (sc. of the
			Red Sea) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχει νήσους μικράς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					3.38
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adj.
			<i>fit for coasting</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ποιησάμενος τοὺς Σιδητῶν παρῶνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					193
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
